People sign in only with the OAuth app of the site, which asks GitHub for their identity and their email addresses, read only (scope ``user:email``); GitHub never asks them to let the site act on their behalf. The GitHub App no longer signs people in. Until the OAuth app is set, nobody can sign in: the people who run the site enter it on ``/setup/oauth-app/`` with the setup code of the log. The addresses that GitHub verified are kept at every sign-in.
